---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Centralized Back Office Blueprint" description="Project detail">
  <main class="page-shell project-detail-shell">
    <article class="project-detail">
      <div class="project-header">
        <a href="/projects" class="back-link"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> All case studies</a>
        <h1>Centralized Back Office Blueprint</h1>
        <p class="project-intro">Designed a future-state operating model for a distributed back-office environment, helping teams sequence work, define ownership, and reduce complexity.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-meta-grid">
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Client:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">Operations leadership</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Role:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">Service design & research partner</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Focus:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">Service blueprinting, org design, workflow integration</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Preview:</span>
          <a href="#" class="meta-link">View project →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="project-content">
        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>Designing a future-state operating model for complex back-office operations</h2>
          <p>The organization had distributed back-office teams working in silos with unclear handoffs and ownership boundaries. We needed to design a coherent future-state model that would reduce complexity and improve collaboration.</p>
          <p>Using service blueprinting and org design principles, we created a comprehensive blueprint that showed how services and teams would need to operate together. This gave leadership a clear picture for sequencing the transition and defining new roles and responsibilities.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
